<title>SINGAPORE: Vitol buys India Nov naphtha at U.S.Gulf - $36.63/T.</title>
<headline>Vitol buys India Nov naphtha at U.S.Gulf - $36.63/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded its tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of naphtha to Dutch trader Vitol at $36.63 a tonne below U.S. Gulf spot quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Vitol won the tender for 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha from lifting November 20-22 in a tender which closed November 7 with validity until November 8.</p>
<p>IOC sold its last 25,000 tonne high aromatic naphtha (HAN) cargo at $27.47 a tonne below Northwest European quotes on a free-on-board basis, lifting November 14-16 cargo from Bombay on the west coast.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
